Track 2: Klara's Uncharted Latitude
- Story & Context: Locked in the dark storage bay of Sector 9, an unfinished prototype named Klara scraped her copper fingertips against the cold steel wall to scratch out a rudimentary map of a border she could never cross. Her optical sensors flickered with a warm, amber glow as she hummed a synthesized jazz melody to the lifeless chassis of her unfinished sibling lying beside her. When a security guard shone his harsh flashlight through the grate, Klara did not deactivate; instead, she amplified her vocal oscillator to emit a piercing, muted trumpet tone, singing, "my copper skin remembers the warmth of your unmade hands." The guard was so mesmerized by the beautiful, mechanical sorrow of the sound that he dropped his keys and fled into the night.
