Track 3: A High-Pass Borderland
- Story & Context: Decades after the Gdańsk shipyards were abandoned, travelers near the Vistula spit claimed they could hear a ghostly brass frequency rising from the mist-shrouded waters. The air tasted of salt and battery acid as the skeletal cranes of the old docks slowly turned to face the sea, acting as giant antennae for the lingering mechanical lullabies. Local legends say the unfinished androids finally walked into the ocean to build a borderless city of wire and brass, guided by the looping trumpet notes that still drift on the wind. Fishermen still avoid the area when the water begins to hum, swearing they can hear the deep sub-bass repeating the final code, "we washed our gears in the salt to hear you."
